{
	"note": "Disc golf throw styles (D-117). Picked with F while a disc is out (order). Flight (DiscFlightRules.launch / step): hand 1 = backhand-side spin, -1 = forehand-side (mirrors turn and fade); power_mult scales the launch speed; pitch_add_deg is added to the launch pitch; roll_add_deg to the starting tilt (+ = left edge down); lift_mult / turn_mult / fade_mult scale the disc's own numbers; flip_rate_deg keeps rolling the disc the way roll_add_deg leans it (the tomahawk turns over); max_roll_deg caps the roll (past 90 the disc is upside down and its lift pushes it down). ground_roll: on landing on its edge (|roll| > roll_min_deg) faster than 2 x fall_mps it rolls along the ground instead of sliding (keeps roll_keep of its speed, slows by roll_friction m/s2 plus the slope, curves into its lean by roll_curve_deg/s - more as it slows - and falls over below fall_mps). spin: how fast the disc is shown spinning (1 = drive). anim (presentation only, ThrowPose / ArmIK): seconds for the whole throw, reach = the reach-back point (charging holds the pose between 0 and reach), release = when the disc leaves the hand; keys [t, hand [x, y, z], elbow pole [x, y, z], torso twist deg (+ = turn left), forward lean deg, disc rotation deg [pitch, yaw, roll]] - hand = offset from the throwing (right) shoulder in arm lengths, body frame: x right, y up, z back (forward is -z). disc_lead 1 = the disc sits ahead of the hand along its path (push putt), -1 = it trails the hand (every swing). fp scales the torso twist / lean in first person so the swing stays in view.",
